    {
      "id": "claim_acf1b9e3d4bc4de7bcc66f6d64db0d5c",
      "statement": "emotionDisplayOf(emotion) is the single-vote display derivation: a user-marked song returns the user's tags with null ratios and HIGH confidence, an empty curve returns empty tags/ratios with HIGH confidence, and otherwise it performs exactly one EmotionGroup.voteRatios over compensatedCurve with anchorsFor(modelVersion) and derives categoriesFrom(vote) tags, the tag-ratio list, and the top ratio that decides SPREAD/MIXED/HIGH. Callers needing tags, ratios and confidence together must call it once, because deriving the three separately re-votes the same curve 3–4 times and re-materializes compensatedCurve on every access; the library list path (EmotionViewModel.buildRows) still makes two passes (emotionTagsOf plus emotionConfidenceLevelOf) since it needs only names and the level.",
